1. Objective

The purpose of the data model is to define a structured format for storing newly submitted bug reports and historical software defects.

The data model supports:

- Bug report submission
- Error and stack trace storage
- Historical defect storage
- Semantic search
- RAG retrieval
- AI agent analysis
- Diagnosis results
- Fix recommendations
 bug report represents a newly submitted software defect.

The proposed bug report structure contains the following fields:

| Field | Data Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| submission_id | String | Unique identifier for the submitted bug |
| title | String | Short title of the bug |
| description | Text | Detailed description of the problem |
| stack_trace | Text | Stack trace associated with the failure |
| error_logs | Text | Error and application logs |
| component | String | Software component affected |
| severity | String | Severity level of the bug |
| priority | String | Priority assigned to the bug |
| file_name | String | Name of uploaded file, if applicable |
| file_type | String | Type of uploaded file |
| status | String | Current processing status |
| created_at | DateTime | Submission date and time |

