6. Knowledge Base Chunk Schema

Historical defect records are divided into smaller meaningful chunks before embedding generation.

Each chunk contains the text and relevant metadata.

Field	Data Type	Description
chunk_id	String	Unique identifier for the chunk
bug_id	String	Related historical bug ID
project	String	Source project
chunk_type	String	Type of chunk
content	Text	Text contained in the chunk
component	String	Affected component
severity	String	Bug severity
priority	String	Bug priority
source	String	Original dataset/source
7. Chunk Types

The proposed chunk types are:

Description Chunk

Contains the main description of the historical bug.

Stack Trace Chunk

Contains technical stack trace information.

Comment Chunk

Contains useful historical comments and discussions.

Resolution Chunk

Contains the final resolution information.

Fix Information Chunk

Contains information about the solution or code fix.

8. Example Knowledge Base Chunk
{
  "chunk_id": "CHUNK-0001",
  "bug_id": "MOZ-10245",
  "project": "Mozilla",
  "chunk_type": "resolution",
  "content": "The issue was fixed by adding null validation before accessing profile data.",
  "component": "Profile Management",
  "severity": "Major",
  "priority": "High",
  "source": "Mozilla Historical Defect Dataset"
}
9. Embedding Data

After chunking, the textual content of each chunk is converted into a numerical vector using an embedding model.

The proposed embedding model is:

all-MiniLM-L6-v2

The embedding record can contain:

Field	Description
embedding_id	Unique embedding identifier
chunk_id	Related chunk identifier
vector	Numerical vector representation
model	Embedding model used
created_at	Embedding creation time
10. Vector Store Metadata

The vector index stores embeddings while metadata is maintained to identify the original historical defect.

Example:

{
  "chunk_id": "CHUNK-0001",
  "bug_id": "MOZ-10245",
  "project": "Mozilla",
  "chunk_type": "resolution",
  "severity": "Major",
  "priority": "High"
}

This metadata allows retrieved vectors to be mapped back to their original defect information.

11. Diagnosis Result Schema

The final diagnosis produced by the system can be represented using the following structure:

Field	Data Type	Description
diagnosis_id	String	Unique diagnosis identifier
submission_id	String	Related bug submission
category	String	Bug category
severity	String	Estimated severity
priority	String	Estimated priority
affected_component	String	Affected component
error_analysis	Text	Analysis of errors/logs
similar_bugs	Array	Retrieved historical bugs
root_cause	Text	Probable root cause
recommendation	Text	Suggested fix
debugging_steps	Array	Suggested debugging steps
confidence	Float	Confidence score
created_at	DateTime	Diagnosis timestamp
