15. Data Model Design Principles

The data model follows these principles:

Structured Data
Bug information is stored using predefined fields.
Metadata Preservation
Important metadata is retained with historical defect chunks.
Traceability
Retrieved chunks can be traced back to their original bug reports.
Semantic Retrieval
Text content can be converted into embeddings for similarity search.
Extensibility
Additional fields and agent outputs can be added in future milestones.
Separation of Data
Newly submitted bugs and historical defects are maintained as separate logical data entities.
